        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T22:11:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alright, I don\u0027t think there is harm in always checking. The spec just says it is a \u0027shall\u0027 for FRS, but of course we \u0027may\u0027 query it as much as we want.\n\nPlus, we have evidence that sink caps may change, its possible they\u0027ll change in the non-FRS case as well so its probably safest to check if we\u0027re relying on this information.",
      "parentUuid": "11108f86_d284caa9",
      "revId": "5b890641d4ba93f0b62419f4d19ef47c1d190fff",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "adf01972_292e5d0d",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T22:14:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re getting into bug mitigation territory here, as a potential caution.\n\nMany 1st gen PD3 FRS products mis-populate their SnkCap(FRS) field depending on whether or not a PSU is already connected. This field /should/ be static.\n\nThen we get stuck into question of how frequently do we need to re-ask \"Jekyll/Hyde\" devices for their identities, \"voting\" based on multiple datapoints, etc.\n\nSince devices cannot spontaneously generate SinkCap messages (it may only be in response to GetSinkCap request), I think it makes sense to only probe once after any events that may /legitimately/ impact overall power state of the partner.\n\nI\u0027ll research more about the DUT in the b/ in question.",
      "parentUuid": "5d63ca18_5740fd3e",
      "revId": "5b890641d4ba93f0b62419f4d19ef47c1d190fff",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da12c620_229f328e",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T22:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, for this specific DUT it doesn\u0027t behave correctly. But since we\u0027re in FRS-land, we **shall** check the sink capabilities upon entry to SNK_Ready, which we don\u0027t do currently. The fact that it ends up fixing this device is a happy coincidence. \n\nBut point noted for the non-FRS case. It doesn\u0027t hurt anything to check after a PR_Swap, which is the only time we\u0027ll be adding it with this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "adf01972_292e5d0d",
      "revId": "5b890641d4ba93f0b62419f4d19ef47c1d190fff",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
